1,48,54,58,32,32,32,32,34,96,123,116,111,107,101,110,125,58,32,123,118,101,114,100,105,99,116,115,95,98,97,114,125,32,123,99,111,117,110,116,95,110,97,109,101,125,61,78,96,44,32,101,120,105,116,32,48,32,111,110,32,97,32,118,101,114,100,105,99,116,32,47,32,50,32,111,110,32,34,10,51,48,56,58,32,32,32,32,34,99,97,110,110,111,116,45,106,117,100,103,101,32,99,97,110,32,110,101,118,101,114,32,98,101,32,114,101,97,100,32,97,115,32,97,32,99,108,101,97,110,32,122,101,114,111,46,32,68,101,116,97,105,108,32,108,105,110,101,115,58,32,96,69,77,80,84,89,58,96,46,32,34,10,51,53,51,58,32,32,32,32,97,112,46,97,100,100,95,97,114,103,117,109,101,110,116,40,34,45,45,99,97,110,110,111,116,45,106,117,100,103,101,34,44,32,100,101,102,97,117,108,116,61,34,85,78,82,69,65,68,65,66,76,69,34,44,10,51,53,52,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,104,101,108,112,61,34,116,104,101,32,99,97,110,110,111,116,45,106,117,100,103,101,32,118,101,114,100,105,99,116,59,32,105,116,32,119,105,108,108,32,99,97,114,114,121,32,110,111,32,99,111,117,110,116,34,41,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],"stderr":[],"exit_code":0,"match_count":15,"file_matches":[{"path":"/Users/kimhawk/.local/state/h-mad/grok-audit-surface/run-ab2c85dc2e25-20261024T132452Z/roots/gas-root-d1-s1-szujeqyy/h-mad/scripts/h_mad_new_gate.py","matches":[{"line_number":7,"content":"`TOKEN: <VERDICT> <counts>`, exit 0 on a verdict and 2 on a cannot-judge."},{"line_number":12,"content":"  1. **A cannot-judge carries NO counts.** `WIRING: UNKNOWN` omits `issues=`,"},{"line_number":34,"content":"exit 0 on a write, 2 on a refusal. Stdlib-only."},{"line_number":71,"content":"cannot-judge."},{"line_number":76,"content":"exit 0 on a verdict, 2 on a cannot-judge. Read the token, never `$?`."},{"line_number":78,"content":"Note the shape of the cannot-judge line: it carries NO `{count_name}=`. A zero is"},{"line_number":93,"content":"    A cannot-judge is `{{\"verdict\": \"{cannot}\", \"reason\": \"...\"}}` with NO"},{"line_number":133,"content":"    # cannot-judge is an operational failure."},{"line_number":145,"content":"got wrong at least once — a cannot-judge that carried a count and read as clean,"},{"line_number":252,"content":"            \"subject: a cannot-judge that carries a count reads as a clean zero, a FAIL \""},{"line_number":264,"content":"                \"name\": \"cannot-judge-carries-a-count\","},{"line_number":306,"content":"    \"`{token}: {verdicts_bar} {count_name}=N`, exit 0 on a verdict / 2 on \""},{"line_number":308,"content":"    \"cannot-judge can never be read as a clean zero. Detail lines: `EMPTY:`. \""},{"line_number":353,"content":"    ap.add_argument(\"--cannot-judge\", default=\"UNREADABLE\","},{"line_number":354,"content":"                    help=\"the cannot-judge verdict; it will carry no count\")"}]}]},"locations":[]}
{"type":"thought","data":"The plan names the test"}
{"type":"thought","data":" file `test_h_mad_audit_cycle_slices.py`,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" but the actual file"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is `test_h_mad_audit_cycle_docs.py`."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe plan's end anchor"}
{"type":"thought","data":" `\\n7.` matches the "}
{"type":"thought","data":"test file's `## Putting"}
{"type":"thought","data":" \\`hmad-dispatch\\` on"}
{"type":"thought","data":" PATH` section."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe plan's risk mitigation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" assumes a nonexistent"}
{"type":"thought","data":" file exists. This is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a false platform premise."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The implementer would"}
{"type":"thought","data":" write against the wrong"}
{"type":"thought","data":" test name. I need to"}
{"type":"thought","data":" verify whether the "}
{"type":"thought","data":"slices file is an outdated"}
{"type":"thought","data":" name. I also need to"}
{"type":"thought","data":" confirm the exact end"}
{"type":"thought","data":" boundary in the test."}
{"type":"thought","data":" A wrong filename is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a strong must-fix."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe plan incorrectly"}
{"type":"thought","data":" states that a cannot-judge"}
{"type":"thought","data":" carries no counts and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" exits 0 on any verdict."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The actual h_mad_new_gate"}
{"type":"thought","data":" behavior is stricter:"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a cannot-judge carries"}
{"type":"thought","data":" no counts but exits"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 2, while a verdict "}
{"type":"thought","data":"exits 0. The audit gate"}
{"type":"thought","data":" transport refusal prints"}
{"type":"thought","data":" `GATE: INVALID must=0"}
{"type":"thought","data":" should=0`, which is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a cannot-judge carrying"}
{"type":"thought","data":" counts and presumably"}
{"type":"thought","data":" exiting 2.\n\nThe audit gate's `INVALID"}
{"type":"thought","data":" must=0 should=0` line"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is required by the "}
{"type":"thought","data":"`GATE_RE` regex, which"}
{"type":"thought","data":" mandates `must=` and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" `should=` fields. This"}
{"type":"thought","data":" makes the new_gate "}
{"type":"thought","data":"invariant incompatible"}
{"type":"thought","data":" with the audit gate's"}
{"type":"thought","data":" parsing rules."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe strategy paragraph"}
{"type":"thought","data":" mis-cites the new_gate"}
{"type":"thought","data":" invariant. This creates"}
{"type":"thought","data":" an internal contradiction:"}
{"type":"thought","data":" following the plan's"}
{"type":"thought","data":" guidance would produce"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a token the cycle driver"}
{"type":"thought","data":" cannot parse, while"}
{"type":"thought","data":" omitting counts violates"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the pattern it prescribes."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The specific FR-3 contract"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is clear and matches"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the specification. "}
{"type":"thought","data":"Whether this contradiction"}
{"type":"thought","data":" actually requires code"}
{"type":"thought","data":" changes is still uncertain."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe plan's strategy"}
{"type":"thought","data":" paragraph should stop"}
{"type":"thought","data":" citing the new_gate"}
{"type":"thought","data":" invariant as a pattern"}
{"type":"thought","data":" for this refusal. The"}
{"type":"thought","data":" spec already requires"}
{"type":"thought","data":" exit 2 with counts,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and the Requirements"}
{"type":"thought","data":" section matches that."}
{"type":"thought","data":" A build must-fix is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" warranted because an"}
{"type":"thought","data":" implementer following"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the false pattern would"}
{"type":"thought","data":" emit a count-free cannot-judge"}
{"type":"thought","data":" or exit 0, which the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" cycle combiner cannot"}
{"type":"thought","data":" parse."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe phrase \"exit 0"}
{"type":"thought","data":" on any verdict\" in "}
{"type":"thought","data":"the strategy paragraph"}
{"type":"thought","data":" likely refers only "}
{"type":"thought","data":"to OK, MISSING, and "}
{"type":"thought","data":"CONFLICT exits. The "}
{"type":"thought","data":"cannot-judge case is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" handled separately "}
{"type":"thought","data":"by the invariant that"}
{"type":"thought","data":" it carries no counts."}
{"type":"thought","data":" This suggests the plan"}
{"type":"thought","data":" may not actually contradict"}
{"type":"thought","data":" new_gate after all."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe transport refusal"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is a cannot-judge that"}
{"type":"thought","data":" must carry counts because"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the audit gate's GATE_RE"}
{"type":"thought","data":" regex requires them."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The feature modifies"}
{"type":"thought","data":" h_mad_audit_gate.py,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" not h_mad_new_gate.py,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" so the audit gate's"}
{"type":"thought","data":" own token contract "}
{"type":"thought","data":"applies here. Citing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" new_gate's \"no counts\""}
{"type":"thought","data":" invariant as the pattern"}
{"type":"thought","data":" for this change is "}
{"type":"thought","data":"incorrect."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe audit gate already"}
{"type":"thought","data":" violates new_gate's"}
{"type":"thought","data":" \"no counts\" rule because"}
{"type":"thought","data":" its parser requires"}
{"type":"thought","data":" counts. The plan should"}
{"type":"thought","data":" not instruct the implementer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to follow that invariant"}
{"type":"thought","data":" for this gate. This"}
{"type":"thought","data":" creates an Axis A contradiction:"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the Requirements section"}
{"type":"thought","data":" matches the specification,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" but the strategy paragraph"}
{"type":"thought","data":" adds a conflicting "}
{"type":"thought","data":"pattern."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe phrase \"Patterns"}
{"type":"thought","data":" followed\" is prescriptive,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" so the contradiction"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is a hard gap. The "}
{"type":"thought","data":"implementer would emit"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a count-free `GATE:"}
{"type":"thought","data":" INVALID` token that"}
{"type":"thought","data":" GATE_RE rejects, breaking"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the cycle mapping. "}
{"type":"thought","data":"This confirms Must-fix."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe plan's \"exit 0"}
{"type":"thought","data":" on any verdict\" invariant"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is imprecise. The signal"}
{"type":"thought","data":" discipline invariant"}
{"type":"thought","data":" requires exit 0 only"}
{"type":"thought","data":" for PASS or FAIL verdicts,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and non-zero exits "}
{"type":"thought","data":"only for operational"}
{"type":"thought","data":" errors. The audit gate's"}
{"type":"thought","data":" GATE INVALID line exits"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 2, which aligns with"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the existing audit "}
{"type":"thought","data":"gate's operational behavior"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and new_gate's cannot-judge"}
{"type":"thought","data":" contract. FR-3 explicitly"}
{"type":"thought","data":" specifies exit 2 for"}
{"type":"thought","data":" this refusal."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe transport refusal"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is a cannot-judge rather"}
{"type":"thought","data":" than a FAIL, so exiting"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 2 is correct and consistent"}
{"type":"thought","data":" with new_gate. The "}
{"type":"thought","data":"only remaining contradiction"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is the \"no counts\" "}
{"type":"thought","data":"invariant against FR-3's"}
{"type":"thought","data":" required must=0 should=0"}
{"type":"thought","data":" fields."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe audit gate's `INVALID must=0 should=0` token is safe from misread as clean. The cycle driver checks the verdict word first, so `INVALID` is not treated as `PASS`. The new_gate guard against zero counts only protects consumers that ignore the verdict and judge solely by count values."}
